      "claim": "The controller selects one exact Linux nr0/fd0/len16 task; other idle/spinner-related workers do not create ambiguity unless they also execute that read. It does not require one total task."
    },
    {
      "anchors": [
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-owner-observer/smp_application_syscall.append.rs:3",
        "scripts/application-tests/owner_observations.py:310"
      ],
      "claim": "Native selection requires exactly one Delivered read16 and actual response claim/worker. Owner parsing binds the original application/delivery/claim/worker/TID and allows other complete inventory rows."
    },
    {
      "anchors": [
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-owner-observer/stability_observer.rs:5",
        "scripts/application-tests/owner_observations.py:224"
      ],
      "claim": "Existing bounded row limits remain8 applications,8 calls per mailbox,16 workers,16 tags,16 pagers. Overflow/incomplete observations still fail. No expected runtime worker count is inferred from one extra guest pthread."
    },
    {
      "anchors": [
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-owner-observer/stability_observer.rs:245",
        "scripts/tests/prepare_stability_owner_observer.py:73",
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-transport-fault/payload-runnable-thread-v1.c:23"
      ],
      "claim": "Counter hooks match actual selected OS/generation and response ledger serial/index/physical span. Other startup/thread claims cannot increment selected counters. The spinner atomic loop adds no delegated selected payload copy, so the current hard profile address0/1/1/1,payload0/0,release0 expectations remain source-consistent."
    },
    {
      "anchors": [
        "scripts/application-tests/owner_observations.py:390",
        "scripts/application-tests/owner_observations.py:453",
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-owner-observer/smp_procfs.append.rs:4",
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-transport-fault/payload-runnable-thread-v1.c:96"
      ],
      "claim": "Terminal/+5 comparison preserves every independently sampled owner row including procfs tids. Additional stable rows are allowed; changed/retired rows still fail. No thread should exit,join,allocate or offload from the spinner before the selected read completes."
    },
    {
      "anchors": [
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-transport-fault/payload-runnable-thread-v1.c:26",
        "scripts/tests/fixtures/stability-transport-fault/payload-runnable-thread-v1.c:84",
        "kernel/rust/syscall_policy.rs:3132",
        "kernel/rust/sched_helpers.rs:5232",
        "kernel/rust/syscall_policy.rs:2843"
      ],
      "claim": "The readiness release/acquire handshake establishes that the real created thread executed. It does not prove the offloaded requester is asleep: wake2 is still an external physical pre-input gate. Scheduling requires no_preempt0, nonidle TID, and NEED_RESCHED or runq_len>1 (ordinary read is not sched_setaffinity)."
    }
